{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters","id":1113919,"title":"Inspirations for Dragon-Blooded games/characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-09T16:04:35-07:00","id":1113919,"title":"Inspirations for Dragon-Blooded games/characters","content":"I know a fair number of people are burned out on <b><i>Naruto</i></b>, but it's still an extremely valid source of inspiration. Leaving the later-series escalation out, Dragon-Blooded should be around the power-level of the ninja, and that power is likewise hereditary. Ninjas and Dragon-Blooded begin life as mere mortals, are sent to school, discover whether or not they have the stuff to become more, and then are given varying degrees of choice about how they will use those talents. Some families and parents are more demanding than others.<br /> <br /> Also, simply knowing one kind of Fire technique -- such as spitting flames from your mouth -- doesn't arise from a broad control of fire, and doesn't necessarily mean that you know how to create a fire-sword or deliver a flaming kick. Jutsu are like Terrestrial Charms in that respect; the fundamental skills necessary for Elemental Bolt Technique and Wildfire Taming Technique are radically different.<br /> <br /> The elemental nations could easily be countries in the Threshold who are distant enough from the Realm to have a completely different society from the Dynasty despite having enough Dragon-Blooded to demand a culture adapted to serve them.<br /> <br /> I really do hope that Dragon-Blooded Dodge includes a few elemental substitution clones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Overwatch</i></b>. Skipping over the obvious Shimada brothers, I ask you to imagine Angela &quot;Mercy&quot; Ziegler as an Air Aspect who favors Medicine and practices Immaculate Wood Dragon Style (which uses staves instead of bows in 3rd Edition). Using her favored Craft Ability, she could design a set of artifact wings to help her fly to anyone in need, and master the healing evocations of the artifact staff she likewise created.<br /> <br /> Ana could be an actual Wood Aspect, using a bow that Angela enchanted to heal rather than hurt. Ana might have deliberately sought to discover a lethal Evocation, to Mercy's pique.<br /> <br /> Reinhardt is a Fire Aspect who favors Melee, Integrity, and Resistance, and practices Earth Dragon Style. Since he isn't a crafter (Craft) and always seems passed over for strategic leadership positions (War) and has no particular sensory abilities in the game (Awareness), he's not necessarily an Earth Aspect.<br /> <br /> That's Torbjorn, of course; a man deeply into the Dragon-Blooded Craft tree and who may have invested little to nothing in the Melee tree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Fairy Tale.</i></b> I hope that Dragon-Blooded Resistance features a Charm for absorbing fire/energy/Essence-based attacks, if only as a Signature Charm.<br /> <br /> A bunch of Exalted out in the Threshold who care more for money than for responsibility and rulership might congregate in a guild like this.<br /> <br /> Natsu might have learned Immaculate Fire Dragon Style from a Dragon-totemed Lunar, who stole the secrets of the Style from the Heart's Blood of a Wyld Hunter who failed to slay him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>RWBY.</b></i> Huntsmen and huntresses sit very closely to the power-level of Dragon-Blooded, and Signature Charms help capture a little of the &quot;you only discover one Semblance&quot; feature of that setting. While the culture of the Great Kingdoms is extremely different from that of the Realm, both feature special schools which train magical children to become future heroes who go out and hunt monsters to keep humanity safe.<br /> <br /> With the Air Aspect anima power and elemental spells, the glyphs and Dust techniques of Weiss Schnee can be emulated with a Terrestrial Exalt.<br /> <br /> Fire-aspected Resistance Charms similar to certain Solar Resistance Charms could allow Yang Xiao-Long to gain strength from damage, as well as to enter a fiery berserker state. The energy-absorption Charm I mentioned earlier would also help emulate Nora Valkyrie.<br /> <br /> Ruby Rose might not trail flower petals behind her, but her Athletics Charms might be marked by cheerfully red embers, and Crescent Rose sits comfortable within Fire's favored abilities of Melee and Firearms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Sword Art Online.</b></i> The Alfheim Online arc featured nine elementally-aligned races of fairies, and the superhuman feats of the previous and following arcs never rose above what Dragon-Blooded martial artists could accomplish.<br /> <br /> Asuna and Klein are both Fire Aspects who favor War, being warriors and leaders of men.<br /> <br /> Agil is a Water Aspect who stays afloat in an uncertain economy, and also takes to battle with his enormous axe.<br /> <br /> Argo the Rat is an Air Aspect who favors Investigation, Bureaucracy, and Stealth. She may wear tiger claws for self-defense, but she prefers to hurl darts from a distance when she has to fight at all. Most of all she prefers to leave fighting to the fighters, and instead sneak around and collect information, which she then sells to the right people.<br /> <br /> Kirito is another Air Aspect, but he might favor Brawl instead of Melee. That not only allows him to use the unarmed attacks he sometimes uses in canon, but also the Steel Devil Style. Indeed, NOT favoring Melee might help explain why he resented the swordsmanship training imposed upon him by his grandfather.<br /> <br /> Silica is a Wood Aspect who favors Melee, Athletics, and Dodge for her courageous knife-fighting, because she was tickling monsters to death with a pig-sticker long before she got herself a pet dragon. Side-materials confirm she actually has Performance skills, even if they never come up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild.</b></i> Link is narratively more of a Solar Exalt, given how completely hopeless everyone else in Hyrule is to defeat Ganon without him. Nevertheless, most of his feats can be replicated by a Wood Aspect Dragon-Blood who favors Melee, Athletics, and a variable third Ability.<br /> <br /> Performance matches very well with the magical ocarina-playing he does in most games, and he doesn't really display any other social Abilities; Presence and Socialize are rather pointless for a man who spends most of his time alone. Meanwhile, he has all the use in the world for Ride, Survival, Medicine, and Archery.<br /> <br /> Make his third favored Ability Occult and make his ocarina (or Sheikah smartphone) a phylactery artifact, and you're golden. Even the magical shapeshifting masks are more likely artifacts than Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Batman.</b></i> Poison Ivy is a Wood Aspect who favors Lore, Occult, and Craft for taking her botany beyond even the level of her own Charms.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dr. Freeze is an Air Aspect who favors Medicine and Craft, which he uses to construct a capsule that keeps his fatally-wounded mortal wife alive until he can find a cure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Log Horizon.</b></i> Shiroe the Strategist could be modeled as an Air Aspect who favors War (for his combat planning powers), Socialize (for the keen understanding of human psychology that allows him to anticipate societal problems and manipulate people into solving them), and Bureaucracy (for organizing societies and guilds into functioning systems). In combat, he uses Wood Dragon Style and a magical staff to help support his allies.<br /> <br /> Naotsugu is a Fire Aspect who practices Earth Dragon Style to serve as the shield of his team. While not sharing Shiroe's talents for War, he has enough Socialize to understand his friend's motives and methods, and more than enough Presence to serve as the friendly outward face when necessary; after all, his real-life job was being a salesman.<br /> <br /> Akatsuki... doesn't fit neatly as either an Air or Fire Aspect. She's not cerebral enough for one or social enough for the other, and none of the other three fit her either. In any case, she would use Air Dragon Style as much or more than Fire Dragon Style, but definitely Ebon Shadow Style most of all.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-10-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:06:09-07:00","id":1113945,"title":"","content":"Today I... was in a room while the recent film adaptation of The Great Gatsby was playing in the background. I would say that the story of the artifice of high society and all of the secrets and lies and mind games could serve as a solid inspiration for games focused on the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters#post1113919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presence and Socialize are rather pointless for a man who spends most of his time alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMaybe your Link spent most of his time alone. I couldn't get enough of finding all of those charming inhabitants of the ruined Hyrule. The dialogue options that they gave for Link paint a picture of somebody with quite a bit of sass to him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:25:55-07:00","id":1113954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1113945#post1113945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMaybe your Link spent most of his time alone. I couldn't get enough of finding all of those charming inhabitants of the ruined Hyrule. The dialogue options that they gave for Link paint a picture of somebody with quite a bit of sass to him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sass is one thing; how much persuading, manipulating, coercing, seducing, and lying does he do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:57:57-07:00","id":1113964,"title":"","content":"<b>Mai-Hime/My-Otome </b> the characters could be converted to a Dragonblooded school setting. Mai is obviously fire, Shizuru wood maybe and Natsuki water. It's meen awhike so I'd have to go back and rewatch it to get a feel for others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:40:23-07:00","id":1113972,"title":"","content":"Maybe another time; I honestly don't want to derail.<br /> <br /> Er, erererrr, somebody particularly Dragon Blooded...<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's this light novel/anime, Kaze no Stigma, about a secret society of warriors who wield hereditary elemental powers to protect Tokyo (and maybe other places) from supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> \u200bI didn't watch much of it, but possibly some of the capabilities they display and the general bullshit family politics of &quot;oh, you're an outsider because you're from the <i>branch family</i>&quot; would be rather useful for inspiring the Terrestrial Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:47:39-07:00","id":1113976,"title":"","content":"A Song of Ice and Fire and similar stories of dynastic conflict are an obvious source for Realm Civil War stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T23:27:50-07:00","id":1114071,"title":"","content":"What about Dragon-Blooded Occult makes you think of Link in particular? Does he sniff out jade or hear dematerialized spirits (but only see them if he has a mirror handy)? <br /> <br /> (Also, why a Wood Aspect? Is it because he wears green?)<br /> <br /> (I haven't played the game all the way through yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T00:27:11-07:00","id":1114080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1113976#post1113976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Song of Ice and Fire and similar stories of dynastic conflict are an obvious source for Realm Civil War stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I had forgotten it's among the resources mentioned in the core book, but GoT is actually a great match for the high court intrigues of the Dynasts. Of course Westeros has no Exalted per se, but there are some similarities to the inter-house conflicts, or the way the Targaryens stayed in power for ages thanks to superior (dragon)firepower. I need to add more civil war to my DBs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T17:39:34-07:00","id":1114326,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Boku no Hero Academia / My Hero Academia.</b></i><br /> <br /> Not the main character, of course, but virtually all of his class-mates. Especially Bakugo (Fire Aspect), Todoroki (Air Aspect), and Kirishima Eijirou (Earth Aspect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:24:56-07:00","id":1114344,"title":"","content":"There's this little show called Avatar... :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:37:42-07:00","id":1114349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114344#post1114344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's this little show called Avatar... :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly surprised this took 10 posts. And from one of the Devs at that! I remember long ago (when the four nations lived together in harmony *rimshot*) when everyone was like &quot;Man, I wish the Dragon Blooded were like Benders, man!&quot; I was among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","user":"Kashi","date":". 07-10-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:46:31-07:00","id":1114352,"title":"","content":"Bah! Low-hanging fruit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:23:23-07:00","id":1114409,"title":"","content":"Any of the magic high-school shows could be tapped for Primary School stories. Irregular at Magic High School, Asterix War, Chivalry of the Failed Knight, Chrome Shelled Rigios, or Akashic Record of the Bastard Magical Instructor. All could be used for what school would be like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:28:15-07:00","id":1114411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114344#post1114344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's this little show called Avatar... :P</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Avatar%28Neytiri%29.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114349#post1114349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember long ago (when the four nations lived together in harmony *rimshot*) when everyone was like &quot;Man, I wish the Dragon Blooded were like Benders, man!&quot; I was among them.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Bender_Rodriguez.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You're right, these two would make <i>awesome</i> Dragon-Blooded!<br /> <span style=\"color:white\">(I kid, I kid.)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:30:29-07:00","id":1114441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114344#post1114344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's this little show called Avatar... :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *distant sound of Grabowski grumbling about who inspired whom on that one*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:33:22-07:00","id":1114444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114349#post1114349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly surprised this took 10 posts. And from one of the Devs at that! I remember long ago (when the four nations lived together in harmony *rimshot*) when everyone was like &quot;Man, I wish the Dragon Blooded were like Benders, man!&quot; I was among them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, most Bending feats can be found somewhere in the Dragon-Blooded charmset in past editions. Just not collected into specific elemental trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T22:34:20-07:00","id":1114445,"title":"","content":"Since the Realm is supposed to be Chinese or something, so I think the genre Gongdau (\u5bae\u6597) will be very good for portraying the <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">intrigue between the Great Houses.<br /> <br /> The basic plot is that in Chinese imperial harem, concubines and empress will be granted a separate place by the emperor, the ladies then try to eliminate each other to become/remain empress and make sure that their son becomes the next emperor (hence the genre's name, battle</span></span> \u6597<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> between the hall</span></span> \u5bae).<br /> <br /> Korean used the same harem system so they makes novel and Tv shows about this too, though I find them to be so soapy, way too much triangle romance plots between the characters while the murder plots aren't as entertaining.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-11-2017, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T00:01:17-07:00","id":1114464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114445#post1114445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Realm is supposed to be Chinese or something</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically its a blending of Imperial China and Rome - with touches of Persia and Britain in how the satrap system works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:49:58-07:00","id":1114544,"title":"","content":"I know it's basically included in Avatar, but I think Korra deserves special mention. I really loved the choreography/animations of the bending. It was really a new level after the already amazing stuff we got to see with Aang and kept me repeatedly saying &quot;I want my Dragon-Blooded to do that!&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:00:08-07:00","id":1114565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114071#post1114071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Dragon-Blooded Occult makes you think of Link in particular? Does he sniff out jade or hear dematerialized spirits (but only see them if he has a mirror handy)?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes me think of Occult with Link is exactly what I said: the ocarina of time and the Sheikah Slate (and possibly the Wand of Winds/Storms), but I am umfamiliar with Windwaker) are shoo-ins for sorcerous phylactery artifacts. The Links who use those artifacts use them to initiate into sorcery and cast spells, but as an Exalt, Link would still need to have the Occult rating and the Charms to be a sorceror.<br /> <br /> I never said he'd have any *other* Dragon-Blooded Occult Charms. He isn't obligated to learn those when he wants to buy up spells instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, why a Wood Aspect? Is it because he wears green? </div> </div> </div>He wears blue in Breath of the Wild, though.<br /> <br /> But I did mention how Breath of the Wild Link would be getting plenty of mileage out of Survival (finding food, navigating the world, surviving the elements, taming horses), Ride (riding horses and anything else he can mount or snare), and Medicine (making his own health-restoring items and rations).<br /> <br /> To say nothing of Archery.<br /> <br /> As I countered to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, BotW Link may express plenty of wit and sass despite being canonically silent, but does he seem to be using much of Presence or Socialize to bend people to his will? Or does he get by on being a nice guy who is also the official hero of the world?<br /> <br /> With his shield, sword, Melee score, archery range, and horse-riding, and all Charms deriving from those, he also doesn't need Dodge Charms so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, no. It's not because his default-blue clothes were green in previous games.<br /> <br /> But even in those games, he does a lot more wilderness-survival, horse-riding, medical self-treatment, and music-playing than he does Presence/Socialize-based social influence. Or even talking.<br /> <br /> He sails in Windwaker, but with the help of a magical, talking boat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:18:59-07:00","id":1114571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114565#post1114565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does he seem to be using much of Presence or Socialize to bend people to his will?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you're bringing it back up...<br /> <br /> \u200bI think there's more to either of those Abilities than doing that; Presence can cover being generally magnetic and inspiring, Socialize into gaining insight into people and societies.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the latter in particular, I would draw inspiration from Breath of the Wild's scenarios, but modified slightly to the change of medium with things such as &quot;you need to put in some work to get people to open up about their problems and feelings&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are more than a few times in the game where people say that they're being open with Link because they get a general sense of him as somebody trustworthy and reliable; if I was running Exalted, you wouldn't quite be able to rely on fiat for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T09:12:31-07:00","id":1114625,"title":"","content":"So a case can be made for Link being either Wood or Fire, depending on which traits you want to emphasize when you roleplay him.<br /> <br /> If you didn't want to emphasize Presence/Socialize, Auspicious First Meeting Attitude and an Excellency might be enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T21:31:24-07:00","id":1114906,"title":"","content":"I'd also argue Warm-Faced Seduction Style as a possibility, considering how many people(?) propose marriage to him!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:33:15-07:00","id":1115044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1113919-inspirations-for-dragon-blooded-games-characters?p=1114906#post1114906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also argue Warm-Faced Seduction Style as a possibility, considering how many people(?) propose marriage to him!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of whom, any Terrestrial Exaltations y'all would hand out to the rest of the Zelda characters?<br /> <br /> Even the ones you would sooner think of as Celestials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:14:43-07:00","id":1115316,"title":"","content":"Zelda just isn't a franchise that has exceptional cast or group. This is why solar's actually work better most of the people are going to be singular with a bunch of Hangers On. Doesn't quite work aside from power level for the terrestrial exalted and really not even then.<br /> <br /> <br /> but I want to participate and I love talking about Zelda meeting Exalted so I'll try. Honestly I think the closest way to translate the Goron's would be an equivalent of breeding Wyld mutants. They seem to be most resembling a combination of turtles or armadillos if you need to use a animal in order to make them beastmen.<br /> <br /> Zora are pretty obviously fish people and we have a number of such already. However they don't seem to have a full-on society or be amphibious. In this probably want to say that they are one of the just weird races that occupy the ocean or fresh water. Chances are they are the byblows of a god. It's just lucky for them they got patronage and sponsorship so instead of being wiped out or forced Underground they more or less got to live as a relatively small Society with very very strict breeding restrictions. Also I don't know for certain but I think that they strongly require a guardian beast in the form of their Patron deity Lord jabu jabu.<br /> <br /> Alright alright to terrestrial exalted that come from Zelda. Okay well here's one that I'm pretty sure everyone will get.<br /> <br /> All ninja versions of Impa are going to be air aspect Dragon Blood. The classical hag could be pretty much anyone. But it seems Espionage work along with their tendency towards implied Grace and skill as well as stealth what work even if they no longer are bodybuilders in tight spandex.<br /> <br /> The postman I would guess would be an earth aspect. I guess? It's just the element I associate with him. He'd have to be a fire aspect for the speed but I just don't see how he could be all that destructive. He's very Swift and quick by just don't see him being all that fiery or having an ill temper. Then again it's kind of a problem overall<br /> <br /> The girl tracker in Twilight Princess she was an Explorer and a trained soldier. That sounds to me like she might be a member of House tepet but it doesn't feel right that she would be scorned for being born a girl considering that women have been generals and soldiers in that house for a long time. In terms of aspect she gives off a very solid feel but she's also associated with the snow region. I guess another wood aspect. That way she can take advantage of survival and in some ways we could tie it into how house tepet, which is more of an air house, might have a problem with how she was born. More so because she ended up being more of a ranger than she was a super General<br /> <br /> Beedle is likely an earth aspect though he really really loves his vehicle and toys. He also likes collecting things and selling them. He's most certainly an outcast though whether this is because he was disowned or he just exalted out in the sticks I don't know.<br /> <br /> The thing with Tingle is he's constantly dressing up and making a presentation of something that he is not. Well at the same time being a grown man who refuses to be mature. So we probably want him acting in contrast to his aspect. Now between the green and his association with balloons you would think that he would be an air aspect or wood aspect. That means we have to make him, in order to be contrary, a fire aspect an Earth aspect or a water aspect. Let's go with water aspect. None of the skills he's actually displaying are in aspect for him then. And considering he should have a focus on bureaucracy and he's actually rather gifted at it in the terms of banking and various business ventures but his enthusiasm is usually for some Goofy passion project. He's actually a halfway decent inventor and can mix his own explosives and other things. But his real skill is always turning Ventures into coinage<br /> <br /> Agatha the bug collecting princess is despite the color and obvious animal Association either going to be a water aspect or a fire aspect. The main thing is she's very very passionate about the thing that she loves and she's redesigned herself entirely about it.<br /> <br /> Okay so now we're running into a bit of a problem. There's not a lot of named characters in Zelda and those that are usually too weak that I ever associate them with any exalted, even the least of which who are world shaking Heroes. I mean can you imagine Ingo or Talon being considered terrestrial exalted? The princes of Earth@ One runs basic if prestigious farm and the other had to kowtow to Ganon in order to wear a fancy cuff. They just don't seem in many ways heroic enough to be Terrestrial exalted. Then again there's nothing that saying that the dragon blooded can't be relative Duds.<br /> So let's go with the idea that the two brothers- oh wait a minute I forgot Ingo isn't really related to Talon. Okay so I guess Talon and his daughter are Earth aspects. No Talon is too unaware. Malon is an earth aspect but Talon is her mortal father! The mother left them not by death but by just leaving. She di